    "result_text": "The suite is green. There's only one test file (`AcceptanceTest`) and it passes along with the full build.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change rejects a supplied `registrationDate` that is later than the server's current date with a `400 Bad Request`.\n\nIn `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`, the create-owner flow already resolved the effective registration date (using `LocalDate.now()` when none was supplied). I added a guard so that when a date **is** supplied and it's after today, the request is rejected before any further processing:\n\n```java\nLocalDate registrationDate = ownerFieldsDto.getRegistrationDate();\nif (registrationDate == null) {\n    registrationDate = LocalDate.now();\n}\n// Reject a supplied registration date that lies in the future (later than the\n// server's current date): an owner cannot be registered ahead of time.\nelse if (registrationDate.isAfter(LocalDate.now())) {\n    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);\n}\nregistrationDate = toBusinessDay(registrationDate);\n```\n\nUsing `else if` ensures the check only fires for a client-supplied date, never for the server-defaulted one. The acceptance test `errorRejectsFutureDate` (posts `registrationDate: \"2999-01-01\"` and expects 400) passes, and the full `./mvnw test` build succeeds.",
